From 187e90d1b81435361d3c02f9462154d47e2881e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:04:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [RetroPlayer] Hide Save / Load for games that can't save
 their state

Emulators that report a savestate size of 0, such as the Switch ones,
still got Save / Load in the in-game menu, and New save there showed
"An unknown error has occurred".

RetroPlayer.SupportsSavestates is false once the playing client has run
for about ten seconds and still gives no savestate size, as some only
give one once they have booted, and Estuary hides Save / Load then, as
it already hides Cheats and Discs. The OSD asks the client as it opens,
so the condition reads that answer instead of calling into the add-on
on every frame.

(cherry picked from commit 76ea9b7cac5252f1501030b4c5b57dc9552aea24)
